```json
{
  "type": "pipeline",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "create_agent",
      "name": "Create stock-abc agent with schedule trigger and notification",
      "plugin": "agents",
      "action": "create",
      "args": {
        "name": "stock-abc",
        "description": "Watch inventory item ABC-123 and open a refill ticket for 50 units when stock drops below 10",
        "tln_source": "workflow \"check_stock\" {\n  step \"get_item\" {\n    mcp \"testdb\" action=\"testdb__get_item\" barcode=\"ABC-123\"\n  }\n  \n  on \"stock_low\" {\n    when current_stock < 10\n    workflow \"refill\" {\n      step \"create_ticket\" {\n        mcp \"testdb\" action=\"testdb__create_ticket\" barcode=\"ABC-123\" qty=50\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nstore {\n  current_stock = get_item.current_stock\n  barcode = get_item.barcode\n  name = get_item.name\n}\n\non \"stock_low\" when current_stock < 10 {}",
        "triggers": [
          {
            "type": "schedule",
            "interval": "10s"
          }
        ],
        "notify": true,
        "escalate": false
      },
      "depends_on": []
    }
  ]
}
```

I've created the **stock-abc** agent with the following configuration:

- **Polling**: Checks inventory item ABC-123 every 10 seconds using the testdb MCP server
- **Trigger**: When `current_stock` drops below 10, it automatically opens a refill ticket for 50 units
- **Notification**: Enabled (`notify: true`), so you'll see a message in chat when the agent fires and creates a ticket
- **Tln Source**: The agent evaluates the flat response object directly (barcode, name, current_stock at top level) and fires an `on "stock_low"` block when the stock condition is met

The agent is now active and will monitor your inventory continuously. You'll receive a notification in chat whenever the refill ticket is created due to low stock.

input.tln_source:
on change attr "current_stock" {
  when prev_value >= 10 and new_value < 10
  workflow "Refill low stock ABC-123"
}

workflow "Refill low stock ABC-123" {
  step "create_ticket" {
    mcp "testdb" "testdb__create_ticket" {
      barcode "ABC-123"
      qty 50
    }
  }
}
